\section{Executive Summary}
% =====================================================================

A comprehensive Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT) engagement was conducted on the VajraKavach platform over three days (April 5--7, 2026). The assessment covered the full stack: FastAPI backend, React frontend, Nginx reverse proxy, PostgreSQL database, end-to-end encryption subsystem, and system-level service resilience.

\subsection{Scope}
\begin{itemize}[nosep]
  \item \textbf{Backend:} FastAPI (Python 3.10), REST API endpoints, authentication, authorization, WebSocket real-time messaging
  \item \textbf{Frontend:} React 18 + Vite, client-side E2E encryption (RSA-4096 + AES-256-GCM)
  \item \textbf{Infrastructure:} Nginx 1.18, TLS 1.2/1.3, PostgreSQL 14, systemd service management
  \item \textbf{Testing Types:} Static code analysis, dynamic live testing, dependency CVE scanning, automated scanner verification
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Methodology}
Testing followed the OWASP Testing Guide v4.2 and OWASP Top 10 (2021) frameworks:
\begin{enumerate}[nosep]
  \item Static source code review across all backend routes, middleware, services, and frontend utilities
  \item Dynamic testing of live endpoints: header analysis, CORS, JWT attacks, brute force, IDOR, injection payloads
  \item Automated scanning: nmap (port + vulnerability scripts), testssl.sh, Nikto, sqlmap, Wapiti, Gobuster
  \item Dependency vulnerability scanning: \texttt{pip-audit} (Python), \texttt{npm audit} (JavaScript)
  \item Service resilience verification: systemd watchdog, health check timer, kernel panic recovery
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Summary of Findings}

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{|>{\columncolor{critical}\color{white}\bfseries}c|>{\columncolor{high}\color{white}\bfseries}c|>{\columncolor{medium}\color{white}\bfseries}c|>{\columncolor{low}\color{white}\bfseries}c|>{\columncolor{info}\color{white}\bfseries}c|}
\hline
Critical & High & Medium & Low & Info \\
