\newpage
\section{Positive Security Controls}
% =====================================================================

The following security measures were correctly implemented:

\begin{itemize}[nosep]
  \item \textbf{TLS 1.2/1.3} with AEAD cipher suites + HSTS (1-year max-age)
  \item \textbf{Argon2id} password hashing (PHC winner, memory-hard)
  \item \textbf{TOTP-based 2FA} mandatory for all users, encrypted secret storage
  \item \textbf{JWT security:} Short expiry (15 min), IP binding, type enforcement, DB-backed revocation
  \item \textbf{E2E encryption:} RSA-4096 OAEP + AES-256-GCM hybrid scheme
  \item \textbf{PBKDF2} with 250,000 iterations for client-side key derivation
  \item \textbf{Resume encryption at rest:} Fernet (AES-128-CBC + HMAC-SHA256)
  \item \textbf{Digital signatures:} RSA-PSS with SHA-256 for message authenticity
  \item \textbf{Blockchain audit logging:} SHA-256 hash chains + Merkle trees + proof-of-work
  \item \textbf{CORS:} Same-origin only, evil origins rejected
  \item \textbf{CSRF:} SameSite=strict + HttpOnly + Secure cookies
  \item \textbf{CSWSH:} WebSocket Origin header validation
  \item \textbf{Rate limiting:} Dual-layer (Nginx 30/5 req/min + FastAPI 60/5 req/min)
  \item \textbf{Connection limits:} 15 concurrent per IP
  \item \textbf{LAN-only access:} Nginx \texttt{allow 192.168.0.0/16; deny all}
  \item \textbf{Progressive lockout:} IP-based, 60 min × $5^n$ escalation, DB-persistent
  \item \textbf{Security headers:} 7 headers including CSP with \texttt{object-src 'none'}, \texttt{frame-ancestors 'none'}
  \item \textbf{SQLAlchemy ORM:} No raw SQL — parameterized queries only
  \item \textbf{Service resilience:} Watchdog (30s), health timer (2 min), auto-restart, kernel panic reboot
  \item \textbf{Automated tests:} 140 tests (unit, integration, regression, frontend)
\end{itemize}

