% =====================================================================
\section{Conclusion}
% =====================================================================

The VajraKavach platform demonstrates \textbf{strong security architecture} with defense-in-depth across all four layers (kernel/OS, Nginx, application, database). Across two rounds of assessment:

\begin{itemize}[nosep]
  \item \textbf{42 vulnerabilities} identified, \textbf{33 fixed}, 2 mitigated, 5 accepted with rationale
  \item \textbf{14 Python CVEs} and \textbf{1 npm CVE} resolved
  \item \textbf{23 mitigation}, \textbf{10 tolerance}, and \textbf{10 recovery mechanisms} documented
  \item \textbf{140 automated tests} verify all security controls
\end{itemize}

The platform demonstrates \textbf{defense-in-depth} across four layers:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{Kernel/OS:} SYN cookies, TCP hardening, kernel panic auto-reboot, systemd watchdog + health timer
  \item \textbf{Nginx:} TLS termination, rate limiting, connection limits, path blocking, security headers, WebSocket proxy
  \item \textbf{Application:} Pydantic validation, TOTP 2FA, JWT IP-binding + type enforcement, progressive lockout, CSWSH protection, E2EE (RSA-4096 + AES-256-GCM), token revocation
  \item \textbf{Database:} Localhost binding, Argon2 password hashing, encrypted TOTP secrets, Fernet-encrypted resumes, SHA-256 hash-chained audit logs, blockchain integrity with Merkle trees + PoW
\end{enumerate}

The remaining accepted risks are appropriate for the LAN-only IIIT-Delhi deployment model. The platform achieves a \textbf{STRONG} overall security posture.

